{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"bd330154e3a1db68b14afc8a4303effb9b0cf07e14ff6831a8f587e67a1550f8","digest":{"component_or_area":"optional dependencies / S3 remote helper","key_entities":["pyproject.toml","src/rebar/_optional.py","tests/unit/test_s3_optional_guard.py","EXTRAS","guard_import","_install_hint","require_s3_helper","MIN_GIT_REMOTE_S3","git-remote-s3","git_remote_s3","importlib.metadata.version","shutil.which","PackageNotFoundError","OptionalDependencyError"],"problem_keywords":["optional dependency","git-remote-s3","S3 backend","version guard","availability check","dependency plumbing"],"propositions":["The S3 optional extra must be declared in pyproject.toml as s3 = [\"git-remote-s3>=0.3.2\"] to keep core rebar lean and only install the remote helper when needed.","A require_s3_helper() function must verify both that the git-remote-s3 console script is on PATH and that the installed distribution version is >= 0.3.2, raising OptionalDependencyError with an actionable install hint if either check fails.","Version parsing must be stdlib-only, extract leading numeric components from the first three version segments, and fail closed on unparseable versions rather than silently passing.","The git_remote_s3 importable package must be probed via guard_import and added as an EXTRAS entry to produce consistent missing-dependency messaging across rebar."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787667133680869001,"uuid":"51ed494b-ff4b-46af-9b1d-461b5f9f8e6c"}